{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 44de715e, for S6: deferral. The CLI keeps a spent\ninvitation secret, and S6 does not delete it.\n\n1. A safe delete needs sync barriers before the unlink, and the store\n   has none today. That is writer hardening, and it costs more than a\n   low finding about a spent secret is worth.\n2. The first half of item 6 leaves S6. The second half stays: the\n   Counter screen clears an invitation from the URL fragment after a\n   failed enrol.\n3. S6's head states the fact in the CLI's custody page: which file\n   keeps a spent invitation secret, and what that secret can still do.\n   Read the membership rules for that sentence. If a spent secret\n   admits nobody and signs nothing, say so. If it can still do\n   anything, tell me before the head, because then the finding is not\n   low.\n4. Writer hardening for the file store is not filed. Your refinement is\n   the record if it is needed later.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}